{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0075523","isObsolete":false,"name":"viral translational frameshifting","definition":{"text":"A process which occurs during viral translation, which involves a translational recoding mechanism called programmed ribosomal frameshifting. This causes the ribosome to alter its reading of the mRNA to an a different open reading frame to produce alternate viral proteins.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"24825891"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"8852897"},{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"860"}]},"comment":"This term is intended to annotate gene products involved in the process of viral translational frameshifting, not viral proteins produced by this translation process.","synonyms":[{"name":"ribosomal frameshifting involved in viral translation","type":"exact"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2017-05-12","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0006452 (translational frameshifting)"},{"timestamp":"2017-05-12","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044764 (obsolete multi-organism cellular process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-05-12","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044034 (obsolete multi-organism biosynthetic process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-05-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044764 (obsolete multi-organism cellular process)"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-28","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044034 (obsolete multi-organism biosynthetic process)"},{"timestamp":"2013-09-28","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0006452 (translational frameshifting)"},{"timestamp":"2013-07-13","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0016032 (viral process)"},{"timestamp":"2013-07-13","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0019081 (viral translation)"},{"timestamp":"2013-07-13","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A process which occurs during viral translation, which involves a translational recoding mechanism called programmed ribosomal frameshifting. This causes the ribosome to alter its reading of the mRNA to an a different open reading frame to produce alternate viral proteins."},{"timestamp":"2013-07-13","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"ribosomal frameshifting involved in viral translation"},{"timestamp":"2013-07-13","action":"Added","category":"XREF","text":"VZ:860"},{"timestamp":"2013-07-13","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"viral translational frameshifting"}],"xRefs":[{"dbCode":"UniProtKB-KW","dbId":"KW-0688","name":"Ribosomal frameshifting"},{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"860"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0075523","ancestorName":"viral translational frameshifting","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"4896","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Schizosaccharomyces pombe"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted","goDiscussions":[{"title":"Viral Processes","url":"http://wiki.geneontology.org/index.php/Virus_terms"}]}],"pageInfo":null}